    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36928" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pŏlyhistor</span></b> ,
			ŏris, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πολυίστωρ</span> (the much-knowing or learned
		man). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The title of the natural history written by C.
				Julius Solinus.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A surname of the grammarian Cornelius
			Alexander</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram. 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 35,
				56, § 115</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
